            "children": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "A higher-order component that adds the ability to measure a referenced node and get that value\nback as a prop."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "Applying "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "inlineCode",
                    "value": "Measurable"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": " to a component will pass two additional props: function to fetch the "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "inlineCode",
                    "value": "ref"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "\nand the measurement object (currently this executes "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "inlineCode",
                    "value": "getBoundingClientRect"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": " returning its full\ncomplement of properties). Both prop names are configurable through the HOC config object."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "Changes to the referenced node will result in new measurements being returned as props. That\nbeing said, it probably is not wise to use this during animation as it may cause unwanted\nperformance issues."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
